  "body": "## What changed\n\n`assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps`, `g76Grid`: J (first depth) is no longer floored to the grid on its own. LinuxCNC's G76 with `R1` cuts J, 2J, ... with the last pass clamped at K, so the control cuts ceil(K/J) passes. The record lays n = ceil(height / first depth) equal rungs (g76Why already holds the equal ladder), so J must satisfy (n-1)J < K <= nJ:\n\n- J is the shallower grid rounding (as before) when that keeps the count;\n- when the shallower J would add a pass, J is the one grid step up, and never a full grid step over the record's first cut;\n- otherwise the record is refused by name: `G76 threading cycle refused - no first depth J on the control's grid makes R1's equal ladder cut the record's n passes (K ...)`.\n\nThe root keeps its outward rounding. Peak, root, I and K are unchanged.\n\n## Golden change, line by line\n\n`crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach-lathe/thread_g76_inch.nc`, one line:\n\n```\n-G76 P0.07874 Z0.315 I-0.004 J0.0314 K0.0944 R1 Q0 H0\n+G76 P0.07874 Z0.315 I-0.004 J0.0315 K0.0944 R1 Q0 H0\n```\n\nWhat this relies on, from the public LinuxCNC G-code reference (G76): J is the first cut depth, K the full thread depth (diameters here, under G7), and `R1.0` selects constant depth, so each pass goes J deeper than the last and the last pass is clamped at K.\n- Old: 0.0314, 0.0628, 0.0942, then 0.0944 (a 0.0002 in pass) = 4 passes. The record laid and the verdict judged 3 (0.4 / 0.8 / 1.2 mm radius).\n- New: 0.0315, 0.0630, 0.0944 (clamped) = 3 passes, the record's count. J 0.0315 in is 0.000004 in (0.1 um) over the record's Ø0.8 mm first cut. The root (X + I - K) is the same as before: never deeper than the minor.\n- P, Z, I, K, R, Q, H and every other line are unchanged. The mm golden (`J0.8 K2.4`) is byte-identical.\n\nThe earlier PathPilot Hub 8L sim run of this golden (PR #517 comments) does not cover the new J: **this golden needs a new Hub run** (not done here, no Hub access).\n\nScan (local script, not committed): realistic records (first depth 0.05-0.5 mm, height 0.3-2 mm, four minor diameters, the stream's lattice) - the old rule mis-stated 2.7% of inch records; the new rule miscounts none and refuses none in either unit. Refusals are reached only by records with many tiny rungs (e.g. 0.15 deep in rungs of 0.012, inch) or a lattice disagreement on the crest.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/lathe_post_tormach_g76_ladder.rs`:\n- `g76_words_cut_exactly_the_records_passes_in_mm_and_inch` - parses the posted J/K as grid steps, counts ceil(K/J) and asserts it equals both the G33 pass count of the same document and ceil(height / first depth) of its record; asserts J is under one grid step over the record's first cut.\n- `g76_refuses_by_name_when_no_grid_j_cuts_the_records_passes` - mm: crest +2 um (inside the lattice allowance) makes K 2.402, refused (J 0.801 would be a full step heavy); inch: 0.15 deep in 0.012 rungs, K 118 steps, no whole J with 12J < 118 <= 13J, refused.\n\nUpdated: `a_thread_posts_as_one_g76_block_with_the_option_in_mm_and_inch` (inch line J0.0315, golden regenerated).\n\nMutation checks (each mutation applied, suites run, file restored and touched):\n- delete `if (j < lo) j = lo;` -> both new tests red (and the golden test);\n- delete the refusal `return { why: ... }` line -> refusal test red;\n- drop the `j <= hi` half of the refusal condition -> refusal test red (inch case);\n- drop the `j - jRec < 1` half -> refusal test red (mm case).\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (post suites 5 s, app suites 1648 s - the shared golden pulled every app suite). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test lathe_post_tormach_g76_ladder --test lathe_post_tormach_thread -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nNot exercised: a PathPilot / LinuxCNC run of the new inch golden; no batch gate (budget).\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #517 and #518 (G76 on both lathe posts): `git merge-tree` with each branch is clean (#517 changes `g76Why`, this changes `g76Grid`), so not stacked. With #517's finish-allowance rule the record's rung count is still ceil(height / first depth).\n- #1667 and #1681 conflict with this on adjacent lines of the same inch golden and `lathe_post_tormach_thread.rs` (their G30 / drive-line changes next to the G76 line): a mechanical keep-both, regenerate the golden at merge.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1619-g76-inch-ladder.md`.\n\nFork synced at v0.19.0 (branched from upstream/main 058e14ca).\n\nChangelog: Tormach lathe G76 (inch) states a first depth J whose LinuxCNC R1 ladder cuts exactly the verified passes (J0.0315, not 0.0314, on the M12x2 fixture); a record no grid J can state is refused by name.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1619\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
